From a9a5341e8e90bf6789a02ac48d6bc59b96e65f96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 14:16:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 033/206] feat(shorebird): wire DDSlotVoters/DDSlotMapping into
 ShorebirdLinker

Replaces the placeholder bytes at +0x40/+0x48/+0x50 with the real types:
unique_ptr<DDSlotMapping>, unique_ptr<DDSlotVoters>, and a RAW
DDSlotResolution* (raw because their ResolveDDSlots frees and replaces it on the
second call). sizeof(ShorebirdLinker)==0x88 still holds -- 8+8+8 replaces 16+8.

InitializeWithDDSlotVoters / InitializeWithDDSlotMapping with their verified
ASSERT strings, plus dd_slot_voters()/dd_slot_mapping()/resolution() accessors.

gen_snapshot --dd_slot_mapping sniffs the first 4 bytes for the DDSlotVoters
magic. EVERY failure path is loud: unopenable file, unseekable file, file
shorter than the 8-byte header, short read, parse failure, and -- critically --
a non-voters file, which REJECTS rather than silently taking the DDSlotMapping
stub path. Without that exit a mistyped filename would look like success and the
sniff branch would be untestable. Buffer slack is 0xFF, never 0x00, because
datastream.h continues a varint while (b <= 127) and ReadStream's own bounds
checks are ASSERTs that compile out in Release/Product.

Observable-state assertion has both halves, the defect from Slice 1: the good
path reports counts READ BACK THROUGH THE SINGLETON (not from a local captured
before the move, which would print correct numbers even if the store were a
no-op), and a bogus input is shown not to produce the same state. Verified
end-to-end against the oracle fixture: "DDSlotVoters loaded: 8 slots, 8 voters",
matching their own "DD table: 8 slots" log.

Negative control: forcing the sniff to `if (true)` still exits 255 on a
non-voters file but reports "bad magic" instead of "neither ... nor". Both
branches exit 255, so exit code alone cannot distinguish them and any test of
the sniff must assert on output -- noted in-source.

Symbol count, product build, same patterns before and after (grep dart::, never
dart::shorebird::; and dart::FunctionKey:: with the :: because bare
dart::FunctionKey matches 26 pre-existing dart::FunctionKeyTraits symbols):
  ShorebirdLinker::   12 -> 16 raw, 4 -> 6 unique methods
  DDSlotVoters::       0 -> 2  (ReadFromStream)
  DDSlotMapping::      0 -> 1  (ReadFromStream)
  FunctionKey::        0 -> 2  (ReadFromStream)
  DDSlotResolution::   0 -> 0  NOT landed -- no production caller exists;
                              SetSlotOwner is test-only until Slice 2b's
                              ResolveDDSlots calls it, so it is dead-stripped.
Raw counts are not comparable to theirs (our unstripped Product build carries
STABS debug-map duplicates); only "non-zero on both" and the deduplicated method
lists mean anything.

Also labels DDSlotResolution::SlotForOwner as test-only/diagnostic and not part
of the reproduced interface, per ruling: it has no counterpart in their binary
and exists solely to verify owner_to_slot_ is written at all.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

